- Evertern Wealth, an independent multi-family office launched by former UBS advisors Jason Stephens and Mic Lundon, expanded its family office platform through a Vontobel deal. (source: InvestmentNews, 2026-07)
    detail: Private wealth intelligence platform FINTRX added 119 family office profiles to its database in the first quarter of 2026, bringing total coverage to 4,503 firms worldwide.
- Modera Wealth Management, a registered investment advisor overseeing $20 billion in assets, launched Mira, a proprietary agentic AI-powered operating platform. (source: Wealth Management, 2026-10)
    detail: Modera developed Mira over two years with OnTrade to automate operational tasks, surface business opportunities and support acquisitions; Connecticut Wealth Management and Mariner have struck similar 
- EXANTE launched a €1 million Gecko Fund offering grants of €10,000 to €150,000 to underfunded open-source projects, citing wealth management firms' dependence on open-source technology. (source: FinTech Global, 2026-10)
    detail: Applications are reviewed quarterly based on adoption, relevance to the financial ecosystem, current funding levels and potential impact.
- Platform leaders for Mariner and Wealthcare said they are meeting with advisors frustrated by SEC reporting requirements tied to new technology, raising the question of whether owning a Form ADV is an advantage. (source: Wealth Management.com, 2026-10)
