- Digital wealth management firm Farther raised $150 million in a Series D funding round led by General Atlantic to scale its intelligent wealth platform. (source: fintechfutures, 2026-05)
- Envestnet announced AI-powered enhancements and financial planning integrations for its Wealth Management Platform as part of its second technology release of 2026. (source: Pulse 2.0, 2026-05)
    detail: The updates, unveiled at Envestnet's Elevate 2026 conference in Phoenix, expand AI automation capabilities and deepen integration with MoneyGuide to help advisors streamline workflows and deliver more
- Envestnet unveiled AI-driven data automation and deeper MoneyGuide integration for its Wealth Management Platform in its R2 2026 release. (source: Yahoo Finance, 2026-05)
    detail: The enhancements were demonstrated on the mainstage at Envestnet's annual Elevate 2026 conference at the Phoenix Convention Center, and are designed to unify planning and streamline financial advisor 
- Envestnet agreed to acquire Vestmark, a provider of portfolio management technology and institutional-grade trading, to meet advisor demand for more sophisticated trading and tax capabilities. (source: Yahoo Finance, 2026-09)
    detail: Envestnet serves more than a third of all advisors across its platforms with $8 trillion in platform assets; Vestmark supports more than $2 trillion in assets and five million-plus accounts.

