THE MARKET: Wealth Management Platform Market
TODAY'S DATE: 2026-10-23

QUESTIONS AND THE FACTS EACH MAY USE
Below, every question is followed by the facts that may be used to answer it. No other fact exists for that question; a figure or company detail not in them must not appear in its answer.

QUESTION 1 (Q2): How fast is the wealth management platform market growing?
Facts this answer may use:
- Market forecast: USD 20.84 Bn (2033)
- Growth rate (CAGR): 15.2% (2026 to 2033)

QUESTION 2 (Q3): What are the latest trends in wealth management platforms?
Facts this answer may use:
- Rapid digitization and a surge in online trading activities boost sales of wealth management platforms.
- Growing adoption of robo-advisory services and virtual financial assistance solutions lets end users manage their wealth more efficiently and drives revenue growth.
- Increasing competition among wealth management firms fuels demand for versatile wealth management platforms.
- Changing needs and expectations of younger client segments push wealth advisory firms to adopt comprehensive platforms.
- Edward Jones is rolling out a hybrid digital investment advice offering to make its wealth management platform more appealing to younger investors. (source: MSN, 2026-08)
- Edward Jones launched its Digital Managed Solutions robo advisor to target young earners and savers just starting to invest. (source: Financial Planning, 2026-08)
    detail: The service requires only $5,000 to get automated investing backed by human advisors, versus Fidelity's $25,000 and Vanguard's $50,000 minimums for hybrid services; Edward Jones is approaching young i
- Apex Fintech Solutions formed an alliance with FusionIQ, a provider of cloud-based digital wealth management technology, to give institutions a faster route to launching modern investing experiences. (source: Yahoo Finance, 2026-09)
    detail: The alliance combines Apex's clearing, custody and brokerage infrastructure with FusionIQ's end-to-end digital wealth platform, intended to reduce integration complexity and shorten time-to-market for
- Vanguard agreed to acquire Altruist, a digital wealth management platform and custodian for independent financial advisors, in a deal valuing Altruist at approximately $4 billion. (source: fintechfutures, 2026-08)
- Broadridge Financial Solutions expanded its digital assets platform to U.S. wealth management firms, giving broker-dealers, RIAs and wealth managers a single environment for cryptocurrencies and tokenized securities alongside conventional investments. (source: InvestmentNews, 2026-09)
    detail: Tom Carey, Broadridge's Global Head of Product and Technology, said digital assets are moving from the margins to mainstream investment conversations; approximately 32% of financial advisors invested 
- Field launched as a wealth management technology company building foundational infrastructure for the advisory industry, led by former Envestnet CEO Bill Crager. (source: Pulse 2.0, 2026-05)
    detail: The launch was supported by two acquisitions through iAltA: BridgeFT, a wealthtech API platform providing multi-custodian data connectivity and normalization, and Precept, whose technology connects da
- Sixty-three percent of RIAs are currently using AI, double the share in 2024, but only one in ten firms uses the technology as a fully integrated part of its business strategy, according to advisor surveys cited at RIA Edge Orange County. (source: Wealth Management.com, 2026-10)
    detail: The figure was cited by Ashley Longabaugh, global head of wealth management at consultancy Celent; Tim Foley of AdvisorEngine and Taylor Ciavarra of Advisor360 said firms should tie AI adoption to cor
- The wealth management industry is entering a new phase after years of heavy investment in digital channels, robo-advice and advisor workstations. (source: Finextra, 2026-07)
- Leading digital wealth platforms are used each month by 9% of Singapore's internet users, nearly three times the share in the next-ranked market, Malaysia, according to the e-Conomy SEA 2026 report by Google, Temasek and Bain & Company. (source: Fintech News Singapore, 2026-10)
- CircleBlack appointed Vikram Chugh, who built the wealth management platform at Robertson Stephens, as its new CEO. (source: Wealth Management.com, 2026-10)
    detail: Chugh said the wealthtech space is very fragmented and that he was drawn to building a unique experience for advisors; according to the 2026 T3/Inside Information Software Survey, CircleBlack had 0.45
- Evertern Wealth, an independent multi-family office launched by former UBS advisors Jason Stephens and Mic Lundon, expanded its family office platform through a Vontobel deal. (source: InvestmentNews, 2026-07)
    detail: Private wealth intelligence platform FINTRX added 119 family office profiles to its database in the first quarter of 2026, bringing total coverage to 4,503 firms worldwide.
- Modera Wealth Management, a registered investment advisor overseeing $20 billion in assets, launched Mira, a proprietary agentic AI-powered operating platform. (source: Wealth Management, 2026-10)
    detail: Modera developed Mira over two years with OnTrade to automate operational tasks, surface business opportunities and support acquisitions; Connecticut Wealth Management and Mariner have struck similar 
- EXANTE launched a €1 million Gecko Fund offering grants of €10,000 to €150,000 to underfunded open-source projects, citing wealth management firms' dependence on open-source technology. (source: FinTech Global, 2026-10)
    detail: Applications are reviewed quarterly based on adoption, relevance to the financial ecosystem, current funding levels and potential impact.
- Platform leaders for Mariner and Wealthcare said they are meeting with advisors frustrated by SEC reporting requirements tied to new technology, raising the question of whether owning a Form ADV is an advantage. (source: Wealth Management.com, 2026-10)
- FusionIQ completed its acquisition of Marstone, a digital wealth technology provider, combining two digital wealth management platforms. (source: Pulse 2.0, 2026-06)
    detail: The combined WealthTech ecosystem serves banks, credit unions, wealth managers, broker-dealers and RIAs, and is designed for institutions seeking investment and financial planning solutions across the
- Digital wealth management firm Farther raised $150 million in a Series D funding round led by General Atlantic to scale its intelligent wealth platform. (source: fintechfutures, 2026-05)
- Envestnet announced AI-powered enhancements and financial planning integrations for its Wealth Management Platform as part of its second technology release of 2026. (source: Pulse 2.0, 2026-05)
    detail: The updates, unveiled at Envestnet's Elevate 2026 conference in Phoenix, expand AI automation capabilities and deepen integration with MoneyGuide to help advisors streamline workflows and deliver more
- Envestnet unveiled AI-driven data automation and deeper MoneyGuide integration for its Wealth Management Platform in its R2 2026 release. (source: Yahoo Finance, 2026-05)
    detail: The enhancements were demonstrated on the mainstage at Envestnet's annual Elevate 2026 conference at the Phoenix Convention Center, and are designed to unify planning and streamline financial advisor 
- Envestnet agreed to acquire Vestmark, a provider of portfolio management technology and institutional-grade trading, to meet advisor demand for more sophisticated trading and tax capabilities. (source: Yahoo Finance, 2026-09)
    detail: Envestnet serves more than a third of all advisors across its platforms with $8 trillion in platform assets; Vestmark supports more than $2 trillion in assets and five million-plus accounts.

QUESTION 3 (Q5): What are the biggest challenges facing wealth management platforms?
Facts this answer may use:
- A lack of customized product and service offerings holds the market back.
- High investment and maintenance costs hold the market back.

